1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,352
This is CrowdPulse.

2
00:00:01,352 --> 00:00:04,893
It lets your audience rate your session while it’s happening,

3
00:00:04,893 --> 00:00:06,693
so you can feel the room, live.

4
00:00:07,593 --> 00:00:11,412
Here’s how it works, from creating a session to the report at the end.

5
00:00:12,312 --> 00:00:13,818
Start in the host dashboard.

6
00:00:13,818 --> 00:00:17,155
Give your session a title, a short description, and your name.

7
00:00:18,055 --> 00:00:21,257
Pick a date and time, then say where it’s happening:

8
00:00:21,257 --> 00:00:25,138
in person, virtual, or hybrid, with a venue and a meeting link.

9
00:00:26,038 --> 00:00:29,206
Choose an accent colour, switch on the features you want,

10
00:00:29,206 --> 00:00:32,097
list it on the home page if you like, and create it.

11
00:00:32,997 --> 00:00:36,645
You instantly get a QR code and a six-character join code.

12
00:00:37,545 --> 00:00:40,234
Put the stage view up on the projector.

13
00:00:40,234 --> 00:00:44,372
It shows a giant QR code, and avatars pop in as people join.

14
00:00:45,272 --> 00:00:49,786
If you listed it, your session shows up on the home page, under Happening now,

15
00:00:49,786 --> 00:00:51,928
so people can find it without a code.

16
00:00:52,828 --> 00:00:55,597
Or they just scan the QR code, or type it in.

17
00:00:55,597 --> 00:00:58,183
There’s no app to install, and no sign-up.

18
00:00:59,083 --> 00:01:02,872
They choose a name, an avatar and a colour, then wait in the lobby,

19
00:01:02,872 --> 00:01:05,248
where a countdown ticks down to the start.

20
00:01:06,148 --> 00:01:09,348
When you’re ready, open the control room and press Go live.

21
00:01:10,248 --> 00:01:12,851
Every phone switches to rating mode right away.

22
00:01:13,751 --> 00:01:15,110
Rating takes a second.

23
00:01:15,110 --> 00:01:16,717
The slider is the default:

24
00:01:16,717 --> 00:01:19,127
drag it, and the face changes with you.

25
00:01:20,027 --> 00:01:22,798
But everyone can pick the style they like best.

26
00:01:22,798 --> 00:01:23,270
Smileys.

27
00:01:24,170 --> 00:01:25,023
Stars.

28
00:01:26,070 --> 00:01:27,179
A rotary dial.

29
00:01:28,670 --> 00:01:29,929
The weather in your head.

30
00:01:30,870 --> 00:01:32,278
A thermometer of hype.

31
00:01:33,178 --> 00:01:35,290
Thumbs, tapped to nudge it up or down.

32
00:01:36,190 --> 00:01:37,406
Or a ring of vibes.

33
00:01:38,390 --> 00:01:42,849
Or just tilt your phone, like a spirit level, and tap Hold when it feels right.

34
00:01:44,190 --> 00:01:48,243
Whatever the style, it all becomes one score, from zero to a hundred.

35
00:01:49,143 --> 00:01:53,260
Tap a reaction, and it floats up on every screen, including the big one.

36
00:01:55,143 --> 00:01:58,023
There’s a live chat, so the room can talk to each other.

37
00:01:58,923 --> 00:02:02,699
Questions go to the Q and A, where the room upvotes the best ones.

38
00:02:03,599 --> 00:02:06,991
From the control room, you can launch a quick poll in two clicks.

39
00:02:07,891 --> 00:02:11,411
And you can put the top question in the spotlight, on every screen.

40
00:02:12,311 --> 00:02:16,326
Meanwhile, the control room shows you how it’s going, every second:

41
00:02:16,326 --> 00:02:20,162
the crowd’s mood, how the ratings are spread, energy, and trend.

42
00:02:21,062 --> 00:02:23,919
Drop chapter markers as you move through your talk,

43
00:02:23,919 --> 00:02:26,161
so later you can see which parts landed.

44
00:02:27,061 --> 00:02:30,432
And a built-in coach nudges you when the mood dips, or spikes.

45
00:02:32,661 --> 00:02:35,240
CrowdPulse can also read the room passively.

46
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:39,402
When the host allows it, attendees can choose to share their attention.

47
00:02:40,302 --> 00:02:43,155
Their camera is analysed on their own phone.

48
00:02:43,155 --> 00:02:44,712
No video ever leaves it:

49
00:02:44,712 --> 00:02:48,408
just three numbers, for attention, positive, and fatigue.

50
00:02:49,309 --> 00:02:53,424
In the control room, the passive signals card blends tab focus,

51
00:02:53,424 --> 00:02:56,756
cameras and a room sensor into one attention index,

52
00:02:56,756 --> 00:02:59,761
shown only once five or more people take part.

53
00:03:00,662 --> 00:03:04,062
It also compares what people say with what they show.

54
00:03:04,062 --> 00:03:08,103
When ratings stay high but attention slips, the coach flags it:

55
00:03:08,103 --> 00:03:09,579
polite, but distracted.

56
00:03:10,479 --> 00:03:13,350
The stage view puts it all up on the projector:

57
00:03:13,350 --> 00:03:17,199
the live gauge, the chat, the polls, and every single reaction.

58
00:03:18,099 --> 00:03:20,087
When you finish, end the session.

59
00:03:20,087 --> 00:03:22,256
Every phone asks for a quick review:

60
00:03:22,256 --> 00:03:26,654
stars, how likely they are to recommend it, and one word that sums it up.

61
00:03:27,554 --> 00:03:28,885
Then comes the report.

62
00:03:28,885 --> 00:03:31,671
A grade, a score, and the numbers that matter.

63
00:03:32,754 --> 00:03:34,888
The mood timeline shows every chapter,

64
00:03:34,888 --> 00:03:37,810
and key moments pick out the biggest peaks and dips,

65
00:03:37,810 --> 00:03:40,114
with what people were saying at the time.

66
00:03:41,014 --> 00:03:45,143
A passive signals section lines attention up against the ratings,

67
00:03:45,143 --> 00:03:47,112
and finds where they disagreed:

68
00:03:47,112 --> 00:03:52,449
engaged but critical in the deep dive, and polite but distracted during the results.

69
00:03:53,349 --> 00:03:58,234
Then engagement, reactions, sentiment, a word cloud, and the Net Promoter Score.

70
00:04:02,749 --> 00:04:08,381
Export it as a PDF, a CSV or JSON, and share it with your audience if you like.

71
00:04:09,281 --> 00:04:10,575
That’s CrowdPulse.

72
00:04:10,575 --> 00:04:14,745
Run npm start, open the host dashboard, and feel the room.

73
00:04:14,745 --> 00:04:15,104
Live.
